w20-checkable-rulebook
----------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code.

Paper (method idea credited)
----------------------------
Tomas Perez-Acle. "No finite rulebook can certify every safe program: an
impossibility theorem for gatekeeping AI agents". arXiv:2611.13367, v1,
submitted 9 Nov 2026. https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.13367
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ , as shown on the abs page.
This attribution credits the author; no part of the paper is reproduced
here, and the sketch is not endorsed by the author. No code is linked from
the abs page and none is used.

Method only: the split between what a finite record of a program's behaviour
settles and what it cannot, and the idea of judging a checkable list by what
it must admit and what it must refuse. No sentence of the paper is quoted.
The paper's simulation figure is recorded only as a token with its offset in
paper_evidence.json and is marked UNVERIFIED.

Repository code reused by contract
----------------------------------
The expiry behaviour mirrors experiments/2026-11-05/w14-silence-expiry in
this repository (main). No file from it is copied here; the tests compare the
mirror with that package when it is present.
